[{:seon.task/name "a-model-call-follows-its-config"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-21: \"this was all done before in the configs and the model execution code should follow the configs that are passed.\" Today `seon.config/provider` resolves base URL, key variable and max-tokens through `seon.config/resolve-in` but reads `:seon.config.ai/thinking` and `:seon.config.ai/reasoning-effort` straight from the global config, so a model or a task cannot set them; root builds one provider at start and every call uses it; `seon.model/default-max-tokens` is a second source of max-tokens frozen at namespace load; and `:seon.task/config` admits only `:seon.config.agent/max-turns`. Correct (one resolver, v1's per-model request construction): each model request's settings (model, max-tokens, thinking, reasoning effort) come from `seon.config/resolve` for that request's task and model (task -> model -> provider -> config), `seon.model` builds the request from what it is handed and holds no defaults of its own (`default-max-tokens` deleted), and a task's config may state the `:seon.config.ai/*` keys its model accepts. Minimal code: extend the resolver and the request builder, no second path."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.model-test/a-request-carries-its-tasks-resolved-settings}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-reply-records-its-cached-tokens"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-10-21 on the standing root: attempt `seon.fences/a-refused-spawn-is-recorded#1` took 13 model calls and 4,123,353 tokens (~317k a call), because each turn now resends the conversation under `:seon.config.render/history-budget` 256000. DeepSeek serves a repeated prefix from its context cache at ~2% of the miss price and reports it in the reply's usage (`prompt_cache_hit_tokens`, `prompt_cache_miss_tokens`, api-docs.deepseek.com, context caching), but `seon.model/parse-reply` keeps only prompt and completion tokens, so whether that attempt cost ~$0.01 or ~$0.58 is unknown, and the history budget cannot be set from measurement. Correct: the completion carries the provider's cache-hit and cache-miss prompt tokens when it reports them (absent when not: absent is not 0), the turn records them (`:seon.turn/*`), and the attempt sums them beside its tokens, so `seon.learn`'s rows can show cost per template. Then set the history budget from turns-to-green against cost."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.model-test/a-reply-reports-its-cache-hit-and-miss-tokens}}]
